WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.927
Week 1: How Spanish Works. spell a name recognize a stressed syllable build a sustainable study loop

2
00:00:06.927 --> 00:00:19.873
Operational objective. By the end of this section you can spell a name, recognize a stressed syllable, build a sustainable study loop. The focus is useful performance, not isolated terminology.

3
00:00:19.873 --> 00:00:28.486
Language system. Spanish sound–spelling correspondence, the five stable vowels, syllables, stress, written accents, and punctuation.

4
00:00:28.486 --> 00:00:37.355
Sound and delivery. Pure a/e/i/o/u vowels; silent h; strong and soft c and g; syllable-timed rhythm.

5
00:00:37.355 --> 00:00:46.631
Core principle. Notice meaning first, then form. Retrieve the new language aloud, compare it with the model, and repair one feature at a time.

6
00:00:46.631 --> 00:01:12.953
Model language. Mi nombre se escribe con cinco letras. — My name is spelled with five letters. La h no tiene sonido. — The letter h has no sound. Escucho y repito cada palabra. — I listen to and repeat every word. ¿Cuál es la sílaba tónica? — Which is the stressed syllable? La práctica breve y frecuente funciona mejor. — Brief, frequent practice works better.

7
00:01:12.953 --> 00:01:22.851
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
